// English strings externalised from QCASLUM.d (translation batch 12).
// DO NOT renumber these references once translations exist.

@1 = ~Have you seen enough? Don't gawk at me. Be on your way unless you're willing to pay me.~
@2 = ~Have 1 gold coin.~
@3 = ~I'm not willing.~
@4 = ~Really? That's... wonderful, actually. I didn't expect it. Most folk hardly pay me anything due to my heritage. I am glad that you're better than this.~
@5 = ~Be blessed, travelers.~
@6 = ~I hope you have a great day.~
@7 = ~The orb just appeared out of nowhere. I'm telling you. Never in my life have I seen black magic like this. Go and see for yourselves, it's just north of here.~
@8 = ~What are you staring at! I'm just a poor gnoll.~
@9 = ~I lost me home because of this thing! My home is lost.~
@10 = ~It cut through your house?~
@11 = ~Yes. One of the damaged buildings was me home. Ask me neighbour, the woman over there. She lost her home too.~
@12 = ~How are you better than me? I work my arse off, working hard night and day, sun or shower, and I barely get any profits whereas you are walking around, scavenging every barrel for loot and you can live off of that?~
@13 = ~Do I look like a fool to you?~
@14 = ~Save your pity. I am not in the mood. I am a hard worker, and I will work for my money! I am no beggar who accepts 'donations'. I shall fight my own battles, no matter how much blood and sweat is involved.~
@15 = ~Thank you so much.~
@16 = ~I... understand.~
@17 = ~Please, kind sir. I have no money. Aid me.~
@18 = ~<CHARNAME>, we need to help poor souls like this. No one deserves to suffer like that.~
@19 = ~This is depressing to see. City of splendour treating homeless people like this. It's heart-breaking.~
@20 = ~Spent no money on this darthiir. Weak, snivelling dogs working hard to gain financial subsidy. Pathetic.~
@21 = ~Here's one gold coin.~
@22 = ~I have no gold. I'm sorry.~
@23 = ~Please, kind miss. I have no money. Aid me.~
@24 = ~<CHARNAME>, we need to help poor souls like this. No one deserves to suffer like that.~
@25 = ~This is depressing to see. City of splendour treating homeless people like this. It's heart-breaking.~
@26 = ~Spent no money on this darthiir. Weak, snivelling dogs working hard to gain financial subsidy. Pathetic.~
@27 = ~Here's one gold coin.~
@28 = ~I have no gold. I'm sorry.~
@29 = ~(The dog stares at you for a brief moment and begins to sniff you. He seems to smell some delicious food leftovers you have in your backpack. Without any hesitation he jumps at you to attack.)~
@30 = ~By the end of this month I shall move to Riatavin. My brother lives there. No Shadow Thieves, no guild war, no banditry, no bigotry, just a plain town.~
@31 = ~It is rare indeed to meet people with fortitude and zeal such as yourselves. I wanted to be an adventurer as a child. Not anymore. My whole family consists of adventurers. You know how many of them is still alive? None. You probably won't live long either. Not that I wanna scare you.~
@32 = ~Salutations. I hope you enjoy your stay here.~
@33 = ~The only proper entertainment in this rotten stink-hole is that arena behind me. I could spent all day watching these amateur fools get slashes and trashed.~
@34 = ~Best opium, best women. This place is paradise.~
@35 = ~Ooohhhh... my head. Pulsating...~
@36 = ~Instead of packing him with steel, you pack him with gold?!~
@37 = ~Couldn't have agreed more.~
@38 = ~I understand you perfectly, sir. Wealth that I acquired comes from ascribed status. I may be a nobility, but I don't look down upon the poor the same way my family would. I wish I could help you more. If you'd kindly accept the donation from us, I am sure you'd use that money wisely.~
@39 = ~Wh-what? Of course not, sir. I...~
@40 = ~Hardly.~
